<title>BELGIUM: Cement maker CBR unit in Polish deal.</title>
<headline>Cement maker CBR unit in Polish deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>ZCW Gorazde, a 51.2 percent Polish unit of Belgian cement maker CBR, has bought a 60 percent stake in Cementownia Groszowice from Poland's National Investment Funds, CBR said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The deal, struck on Friday, had to be approved by regulatory authorities before it could be finalised. It gave no details.</p>
<p>Groszowice's plant, which has annual capacity of 300,000 tonnes of cement, is near Gorazde's plant close to the city of Opole.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
